# Copy to .devcontainer/kit.local.env (gitignored) for settings that belong to
# this machine rather than the project. run.sh reads it after kit.env, and a
# key set here replaces kit.env's. Only PROJECT_NAME and PORTS are accepted.
#
# The name: a template ships PROJECT_NAME=changeme in kit.env, and its own
# checkout still needs a real one. A project made from the kit sets it in
# kit.env with `python3 .devcontainer/set-project-name.py <name>` instead.
#PROJECT_NAME=changeme
#
# The ports: host:container pairs, space-separated, published in place of
# kit.env's. Give each project on this machine its own block, so two
# containers never want the same host port. Uncomment one line:
#PORTS="5000:5000 5001:5001 5002:5002 5003:5003 5004:5004 5005:5005 5006:5006 5007:5007 5008:5008 5009:5009 5010:5010"
#PORTS="6000:6000 6001:6001 6002:6002 6003:6003 6004:6004 6005:6005 6006:6006 6007:6007 6008:6008 6009:6009 6010:6010"
